  ],
  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.125875,
      "text": "Can a share change its name without getting any bigger?",
      "source_sha256": "f8995dd7243530d6101916b797d92c1e05ee8e6352c6a5983317d820e36e3438"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.245875,
      "end": 7.218125,
      "text": "Imagine dividing your half of a ribbon into smaller pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "a1c0e4cef39baeeaef05b09ac31ee85335b1e708684c388a3a89637bf70901c0"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.338125,
      "end": 9.738416666666666,
      "text": "Have you somehow gained more ribbon?",
      "source_sha256": "fba66723d6011351180cbd3cf5a69affd0812eb6e00dcf856dc869d1a666fbe6"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.466666666666667,
      "end": 17.693666666666665,
      "text": "Today, we're learning to recognise, create and explain equivalent fractions: different names for exactly the same amount.",
      "source_sha256": "b1b3dc3717dd03488da4f081b7d5daa5772bfef978b5d63736dfaa60f82258a9"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.3,
      "end": 23.531041666666667,
      "text": "You'll recognise equal amounts, even when the pictures have different numbers of pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "ca61e2e7bf3bc407e64a25a1ad91382bcc55eee0ecc663965bedb0a489b22563"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.733333333333334,
      "end": 27.929,
      "text": "You'll create a new fraction name by changing both numbers fairly.",
      "source_sha256": "d592c0296f63cf19bd795754f6cd006d5482df58dfd44b7319ee26af78a6c14c"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.133333333333333,
      "end": 33.97795833333333,
      "text": "You'll also simplify a fraction, and use a model to explain why its value stays the same.",
      "source_sha256": "a1626cad5e6406d306b34830fa2b209fc017b1b191018e2f11c6fdc28d0976fa"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.2,
      "end": 35.77033333333333,
      "text": "First, choose one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "7e101bd27b3da6ca2ce27baafb76055fd7259335a137a8e746cb201af616b823"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.89033333333333,
      "end": 38.5975,
      "text": "Its parts must be equal in size.",
      "source_sha256": "b9bf48a1ffc5b6d3c73fb0a8c27542e8712625a8731aa2275ae536f2d0cbbf1a"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.7175,
      "end": 43.354416666666665,
      "text": "The outline of the model shows the entire whole, not just the coloured share.",
      "source_sha256": "73d1a9c4a463db9a97e01aa06c1e10c242f158e9c0feae2f017d2b42e2e43f9e"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.86666666666667,
      "end": 47.082125,
      "text": "Here, three equal parts are chosen out of four.",
      "source_sha256": "384340c7a80ec6886d87195982f702328b9f2a1a2cfd4f50da242032f0a6f99f"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.202125,
      "end": 50.97304166666667,
      "text": "The top number, the numerator, counts chosen parts.",
      "source_sha256": "e44912350979e0f4f14884ca88d5e96d596453de0683d8b01cbdefbd2c98836b"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.093041666666664,
      "end": 55.721833333333336,
      "text": "The bottom number, the denominator, tells how many equal parts make the whole.",
      "source_sha256": "05a1025f9d006de9936984495c767ecd74f32f8caac28a6ab28ad75e66a2e319"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.333333333333336,
      "end": 61.5715,
      "text": "If every half is split into two equal pieces, what will happen to the coloured amount?",
      "source_sha256": "0f651c14110f5ebe8177b2449851a003d64bcf71168673881872732af0582017"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.6915,
      "end": 63.94275,
      "text": "Predict its new fraction name.",
      "source_sha256": "8b023e0cc5ed41e2368b857d83079c8c4d8e157a1d15fbe32a944d2dceadd4c2"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.96666666666667,
      "end": 68.58729166666667,
      "text": "Start with one half.",
      "source_sha256": "19cf481299edc04ecdbb4329c7c454b5e87d0b16adda2a8ef35a2baf0f883ead"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.70729166666666,
      "end": 72.548,
      "text": "Split every part of the whole into two equal pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "5a6fe72cf104d0c306204955f9dfea35d3407083a75879f5987c3c9c4f8639de"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.668,
      "end": 75.78104166666667,
      "text": "The shaded half now contains two quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "d10cc5c62a180cb7ef2d1ab576bf03219b74ca3fd54d90083d85551238508b2a"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.13333333333334,
      "end": 78.549625,
      "text": "Split every quarter in half again.",
      "source_sha256": "fbe653b8834db1ca93e8ad4efb6a05add37a197e82a56d6dc6904733f82954c2"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.669625,
      "end": 81.88558333333333,
      "text": "Now four of eight equal pieces are shaded.",
      "source_sha256": "421c5a793d587842c3f3c989f9ab80d246cca35a605348bfeca5c2b9e73d58dd"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.00558333333333,
      "end": 85.81916666666666,
      "text": "One half, two quarters and four eighths are equivalent.",
      "source_sha256": "4d8f112040ab74525e447fcde78471f8a53612b0f88ad9d125a78811b211bf63"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.2,
      "end": 90.31154166666667,
      "text": "Notice the coloured length stays fixed while the boundaries change.",
      "source_sha256": "62866978d23e349c27946e1d3be646ffc1955d9f41f1b4916b052328214a02d6"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.43154166666666,
      "end": 95.42320833333333,
      "text": "We aren't adding ribbon; we're choosing a new way to count equal-sized pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "0682fb0cfb03680574f1a93c133eb9e8c48986c0ff18730e120807d6c6037348"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.1,
      "end": 98.72520833333333,
      "text": "The number rule matches the picture.",
      "source_sha256": "cd5d9ab0c65063cbf119aecf5ef6f8f1b89a0dbbd94db292455020a4fc55c96b"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.84520833333333,
      "end": 103.760625,
      "text": "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the same non-zero number.",
      "source_sha256": "b9a472c55d659c85e1d32384063c732c145f5190e87cc7241c67eff29a135347"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.13333333333334,
      "end": 108.45191666666666,
      "text": "Can you give three fifths a new name with twenty equal parts in the whole?",
      "source_sha256": "45830bc9b799a4bd07c36f10e48ccc38451450c2f00041b8eebec7ca298b578b"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.57191666666667,
      "end": 111.96654166666667,
      "text": "Think about what changes and what must stay unchanged.",
      "source_sha256": "296dc64119011211ee077c824dd59ed93622c48e7aa8f712d32fc90c55a76f54"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.96666666666667,
      "end": 118.58241666666666,
      "text": "For three fifths, multiply both numbers by four.",
      "source_sha256": "1700873487b2280cfae547b2f03e01ce9fd735ded0310c9c4745627807080e7f"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.70241666666666,
      "end": 122.56966666666666,
      "text": "Three times four is twelve, and five times four is twenty.",
      "source_sha256": "c99441dd10422b9fb36885ec2ffabe5a4541fff741af82c2086ae834e08c0e79"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.93333333333334,
      "end": 129.34541666666667,
      "text": "The whole has four times as many pieces, and the chosen share has four times as many pieces too.",
      "source_sha256": "36baff1f84ee40cd25d500bf0b4fa8345d4a1cb912c8bb44a00b4fad9608f507"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.46541666666667,
      "end": 133.37479166666665,
      "text": "Changing both counts together keeps the share unchanged.",
      "source_sha256": "e6a220e9efe4f9d156323f935b9292334c06b981eb3b90365293561e8e504d37"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.03333333333333,
      "end": 138.24004166666666,
      "text": "Equivalent fractions also land at the same point on a number line.",
      "source_sha256": "5c64ff95ec97d2196aee7bea93d656239d4ea4f553cf758127742f19d17a6d89"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.36004166666666,
      "end": 140.86079166666667,
      "text": "They are different names for one number.",
      "source_sha256": "e8559e1f50365c8111fbc16318e03284b5aa85b56ee0b9fc639a46a793c0d44c"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.23333333333332,
      "end": 143.507375,
      "text": "Simplifying works in reverse.",
      "source_sha256": "6e682198eded2ae89ed378dfad0c40ff01bd92fef94a3b209129b262e7f97424"
    },
    {
      "start": 143.627375,
      "end": 148.27604166666666,
      "text": "Group equal pieces together instead of splitting them into smaller pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "aa1873aff56735493dbd16e262142fdec80ed7de8c0e557988364f96f3552004"
    },
    {
      "start": 148.63333333333333,
      "end": 150.77175,
      "text": "Group the eighths in pairs.",
      "source_sha256": "5513fb0295a50c3de063e6045dc9f24ac95670d4f83ae5797db5b7edfb5d43dd"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.89175,
      "end": 153.35304166666666,
      "text": "Six eighths becomes three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "c1342e88624ac5052deb8243d5316c38582cd8ade68f23cbe07783a5a56994d8"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.47304166666666,
      "end": 157.173375,
      "text": "We divided the numerator and denominator by two.",
      "source_sha256": "ee6e9dd30c130ee89424238f657d494da2ea224792d4428e5f40525445710ed4"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.53333333333333,
      "end": 159.39045833333333,
      "text": "Try twelve eighteenths.",
      "source_sha256": "f64c76735190376a17188ec8d685c0395ea120400197b094bf8e9c1725ff2d8f"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.51045833333333,
      "end": 162.77858333333333,
      "text": "Both twelve and eighteen divide by six.",
      "source_sha256": "a34000f02fbe98f07ab3222b2daf106a788a339b57ca2729eccbd3c1d8686ce9"
    },
    {
      "start": 162.89858333333333,
      "end": 167.50991666666667,
      "text": "Twelve divided by six is two; eighteen divided by six is three.",
      "source_sha256": "789b7241b6cd34f67e612144e511249b85b5fdd0fc44a2bb477cecd31a9f22e7"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.86666666666667,
      "end": 172.856625,
      "text": "Be careful: adding the same number to both numbers does not preserve the value.",
      "source_sha256": "6cdefa4c45d177559768acfce2c8f25f72924e48172e8385d4460b7439256fb9"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.976625,
      "end": 176.15695833333334,
      "text": "One half and two thirds are different amounts.",
      "source_sha256": "fb607279aa4a7f120ca45b13c813bf59278badcbace77f1e16171392acc6747d"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.53333333333333,
      "end": 181.451875,
      "text": "Adding one to the top and bottom gives two thirds, not another name for one half.",
      "source_sha256": "e623ead59f477bdec6d185b6e0198c3f3d672c34a84d5842cbee137dc67b5732"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.571875,
      "end": 185.434625,
      "text": "Compare the equal-length bars: the coloured amounts are different.",
      "source_sha256": "de46961bc52b76a2e515daae575887be10f1f2559a09a771398ac04d0e5fdc73"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.1,
      "end": 188.67083333333332,
      "text": "We can also partition a fraction.",
      "source_sha256": "3eb4ecd569542f147756fb5c70512480d869785ec601a0fb8e52fe77a6612e88"
    },
    {
      "start": 188.79083333333332,
      "end": 192.60641666666666,
      "text": "Three quarters is three one-quarter pieces added together.",
      "source_sha256": "6e6c17d2efca9c2c4e160766bfca43d396a0b3a9bd0fd8c26c3fc7c295823b2a"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.96666666666667,
      "end": 198.10258333333334,
      "text": "Two quarters make one half, so three quarters is also one half plus one quarter.",
      "source_sha256": "326c6787d10d34d88a9fea7fbb3e6c7f89f589cb4215c776c39cb3ab1a89ecb1"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.22258333333335,
      "end": 201.563625,
      "text": "Different partitions can describe the same amount.",
      "source_sha256": "332b6b36153c71f4463489ea48361995c5e6c2ce6fed5640cc4135d1c7c23ad0"
    },
    {
      "start": 201.93333333333334,
      "end": 204.96204166666666,
      "text": "Is six eighths equivalent to three quarters?",
      "source_sha256": "a5e1503b50634e6afcc697e8b6d031e3bbacbf1347eb0f40ab5add71db0bc9ef"
    },
    {
      "start": 209.96666666666667,
      "end": 210.80825,
      "text": "Yes.",
      "source_sha256": "4fd86f3edc8903f69a77d80350f24493605f0144399774cb8c10aaff2973b102"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.92825,
      "end": 214.77079166666667,
      "text": "Dividing both six and eight by two gives three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "89e38c676ad50aa95e6d530b83d67f8fc69c9a7653b97166cf9f122efaa56b85"
    },
    {
      "start": 215.13333333333333,
      "end": 219.553125,
      "text": "We set out to recognise, create and explain equivalent fractions.",
      "source_sha256": "4b9c474e8b18041ae295301ea066cf5a3ea8e96392e2a77887e3ed8b0a31ac9a"
    },
    {
      "start": 219.673125,
      "end": 226.14916666666667,
      "text": "You can split or group equal parts, change both numbers together, and check that the amount stays the same.",
      "source_sha256": "35179425a4c76854727a35b09caef103761067b0e1edd7ae81b0840b11af9ab4"
    },
    {
      "start": 226.26916666666668,
      "end": 229.04370833333334,
      "text": "How many names can you find for one half?",
      "source_sha256": "14cab8408d56163c25787a78f1e745b69f3d3f781e30ad4581e87977dc3d59d3"
    },
    {
      "start": 229.16370833333335,
      "end": 231.81404166666667,
      "text": "Explore the practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "d9fcb9b1bfc719df0b354f391fb20e9202e197c3b18118814fc04fffb6128adc"
    }
  ],
